13. Approximation Bounds

Definition 13.1 (Approximate transition cost). Let  \widehat{C}_T  satisfy  |\widehat{C}_T(s,s') - C_T(s,s')| \le \epsilon .

Theorem 13.2 (Decision error bound). Under the static threshold, the approximate rule  Q(s',T) - Q(s,T) > \lambda \widehat{C}_T(s,s')  differs from the exact rule only when

|\Delta Q - \lambda C_T(s,s')| \le \lambda \epsilon.

Proof. The exact rule switches iff  \Delta Q > \lambda C_T . The approximate rule switches iff  \Delta Q > \lambda \widehat{C}_T . These disagree only when  \Delta Q  lies strictly between  \lambda C_T  and  \lambda \widehat{C}_T . Since  |\widehat{C}_T - C_T| \le \epsilon , the disagreement region has width at most  \lambda \epsilon .  \square 

Corollary 13.3 (Three-zone decision rule). Let  C^- \le C_T \le C^+ . Define  \Delta Q = Q(s',T) - Q(s,T) . Then:

· Zone I (definitely switch):  \Delta Q > \lambda C^+ .
· Zone II (definitely stay):  \Delta Q < \lambda C^- .
· Zone III (uncertain):  \lambda C^- \le \Delta Q \le \lambda C^+ .

Corollary 13.4 (Lower bound — uniform edit cost). If every topology edit costs at least  c_{\min} > 0 , then

C_T(s,s') \ge c_{\min} \cdot d_{\text{edit}}(G,G').

Proof. Any feasible trajectory induces a sequence of edits from  G  to  G' . The number of edits is at least  d_{\text{edit}}(G,G') . Each contributes at least  c_{\min} .  \square 

Corollary 13.5 (Lower bound — bounded edits per transition). If every elementary transition performs at most  r_{\max}  edits and costs at least  c_{\min} , then

C_T(s,s') \ge c_{\min} \left\lceil \frac{d_{\text{edit}}(G,G')}{r_{\max}} \right\rceil.

Proof. At least  \lceil d_{\text{edit}} / r_{\max} \rceil  transitions are required. Each contributes at least  c_{\min} .  \square 

