Appendix H. Open Problems in Formal Statement

Problem H.1 (Complexity classification). For which graph classes  \mathcal{C}  (trees, bounded-treewidth, planar) is  C_T(s,s')  polynomial-time computable?

Partial result. Reconfiguration is FPT parameterized by treewidth for MSO-definable problems (van der Zanden, 2015). For some vertex-subset problems, reconfiguration remains PSPACE-complete even for treewidth  \le \ell .

Problem H.2 (PTAS existence). Does there exist a PTAS for  C_T  under metric edit costs when  \mathcal{G}_0  is restricted to bounded-treewidth graphs?

Problem H.3 (Sample complexity). Determine the pseudo-dimension  d_{\mathcal{F}}  for the specific hypothesis class of transition-cost estimators parameterized by a graph neural network.

Problem H.4 (Dynamic hysteresis with stochastic tasks). Characterize the persistence region for  T \sim P_T  with variance  \sigma_T^2 .

Problem H.5 (Option value decomposition). Can the Bellman fixed point be decomposed as

V^*(s,T) = Q(s,T) + O(s,T)

where  O(s,T)  is a well-defined option value satisfying an explicit recursion?

Problem H.6 (Constrained MDP with peak constraints). Does the peak-cost constrained MDP admit a polynomial-time algorithm under any structural conditions on the MDP?

Problem H.7 (Emergent topology). Can reconfiguration policies be learned end-to-end via differentiable relaxation of  C_T ? If so, what are the convergence guarantees?

